    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d307">

                <pb facs="0554" n="540" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg540"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/8–1744</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Admiral William D.
                            Leahy, Chief of Staff to the Commander in Chief of the Army
                        and Navy, to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-08-17">17 August,
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: The Supreme Commander,
                    Allied Expeditionary Force, has proposed the issuance of synchronized orders of
                    the day by Marshal Stalin, General Eisenhower and General Wilson.<anchor n="82"
                        xml:id="d307-f1"/> This proposal is detailed in the telegram attached.</p>
                <p>The Combined Chiefs of Staff<anchor n="83" xml:id="d307-f2"/> consider that the
                    political implications in this proposal are such that, if implemented, it should
                    be handled by the heads of state.</p>
                <p>General Eisenhower has been informed that his proposal has been forwarded to the
                    Department of State and the Foreign Office.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Joint Chiefs of Staff: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William</hi> D. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Leahy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d307-a1.xml" xpointer="d307-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d307-f1" n="82" xml:id="d307-f1-content">
                <p>British General Sir Henry Maitland Wilson, Supreme Allied Commander,
                    Mediterranean Theater.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d307-f2" n="83" xml:id="d307-f2-content">
                <p>The Anglo-American Combined Chiefs of Staff, established in January 1942.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
